From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: a count is derived, not carried
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

agent.sta_count multiplied by the number of controller restarts.

n->sta_count is a running counter - ++ in node_add_sta, -- in node_del_sta and
node_update_stalist - and nothing ever recomputes it from the list it counts.
Our own recovery then seeds it: restore_agents() reads the stored number back
into a node whose stalist is empty, because there is no restore_stations() and
there should not be one. The node comes up claiming N clients with no clients,
and then counts its real ones on top.

Measured 2026-09-06 after three controller restarts:

    node        real                          sta_count   ratio
    corridor    4 (1 client + 3 bSTA)            12        x3
    bedroom     1                                 3        x3
    kitchen     1                                 1        x1  (stored 0)
    hall        0                                 0        -
    controller  2                                 2        x1

Two independent nodes carrying the same multiplier is not drift, it is
arithmetic: 4 -> 4+4 -> 8+4 = 12, and 1 -> 1+1 -> 2+1 = 3. And the one node
whose count is right is the controller itself, the only node restore_agents
skips - "never re-materialize self". The control group came for free.

Sampled over 150 s the numbers do not move, so nothing was going to correct
them: the value is written to the database on every sync, always wrong, and
it is what the node list in the web UI shows as the client count.

Two changes, one idea. The number written out is counted from n->stalist every
time, and the number is no longer restored - which clients are attached is
what the agents say within seconds of coming up, and it is precisely the part
of the model that must not be remembered across a restart.

--- a/src/db/mapc_sync.c
+++ b/src/db/mapc_sync.c
@@ -176,7 +176,39 @@
 	else
 		mapdb_bind_int(st, 10, n->est_thput_dl);
 	mapdb_bind_int(st, 11, n->scan_supported);
-	mapdb_bind_int(st, 12, n->sta_count);
+
+	/* A count is derived, not carried.
+	 *
+	 * n->sta_count is a running counter: ++ in node_add_sta, -- in
+	 * node_del_sta and node_update_stalist. Nothing ever recomputes it from
+	 * the list it counts, so once the two part company they never meet
+	 * again - and they are made to part company by our own recovery, which
+	 * restores this number from the database while restoring no stations at
+	 * all. The node comes up claiming N clients with an empty list, then
+	 * counts its real clients on top of that.
+	 *
+	 * It multiplies. Measured 2026-09-06, three controller restarts:
+	 *
+	 *   corridor   4 real (1 client + 3 bSTA)   sta_count 12   x3
+	 *   bedroom    1 real                       sta_count  3   x3
+	 *   controller 2 real                       sta_count  2   x1
+	 *
+	 * Two independent nodes, the same multiplier, and the one node that is
+	 * right is the controller itself - the only node restore_agents skips
+	 * ("never re-materialize self"). The experiment came for free.
+	 *
+	 * So the number written here is counted, every time, from the list it
+	 * claims to describe. Walking a handful of entries costs nothing next
+	 * to a value that can only ever be wrong.
+	 */
+	{
+		struct sta *cs = NULL;
+		int nsta = 0;
+
+		list_for_each_entry(cs, &n->stalist, list)
+			nsta++;
+		mapdb_bind_int(st, 12, nsta);
+	}
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
 	mapdb_bind_int(st, 13, n->max_mld_num);
 	mapdb_bind_int(st, 14, n->max_aplink_num);
@@ -1500,7 +1532,15 @@
 		n->est_thput_ul   = (uint32_t)mapdb_column_int(st, 7);
 		n->est_thput_dl   = (uint32_t)mapdb_column_int(st, 8);
 		n->scan_supported = (bool)mapdb_column_int(st, 9);
-		n->sta_count      = (uint32_t)mapdb_column_int(st, 10);
+		/* sta_count is NOT restored. It counts n->stalist, and nothing
+		 * here restores a single station into it - there is no
+		 * restore_stations() and there should not be one: which clients
+		 * are attached is what the agents tell us within seconds of
+		 * coming up, and it is the one part of the model that must not
+		 * be remembered from before the restart. Seeding the counter
+		 * without the list is what made it multiply by the number of
+		 * restarts. Left at 0; the first report counts it properly.
+		 */
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
 		n->max_mld_num      = (int)mapdb_column_int(st, 11);
 		n->max_aplink_num   = (int)mapdb_column_int(st, 12);
